# Potomatic — external dependency (read-only)

Potomatic ships as npm [`@publishpress/potomatic`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@publishpress/potomatic) (PublishPress fork of GravityKit Potomatic). It is installed under `node_modules/@publishpress/potomatic/`. **Do not edit** files there in this repo.

- No fixes, prompts, providers, tests, or config changes inside the npm package.
- Need different AI/batch behavior → bump `@publishpress/potomatic` in root `package.json` or change **publishpress/library-potomatic** upstream — **not** agent edits under `node_modules/`.

## What agents may change (PHP and packaging only)

- `src/Translator.php` — `buildCommand()`, flags passed to CLI, dictionary temp dir, paths via `getPotomaticPath()`
- `scripts/setup-potomatic.php` — verify / install `node_modules` (if packaging changes)
- `composer.json` / root `package.json` — version pin and install hooks

## Integration reference (read-only)

PHP invokes the `potomatic` binary with e.g. `--target-languages`, `--pot-file-path`, `--output-dir`, `--po-file-prefix`, `--model`, `--batch-size`, `--jobs`, `--max-cost`, `--api-key`, optional `--use-dictionary` + `--dictionary-path`.

PublishPress-specific terms: `config/dictionaries.json` + env overrides → temp dictionary JSON for Potomatic (built in PHP, not in the npm package config tree).

## If task sounds like “fix Potomatic”

Stop. Implement in PHP (wrappers, post-process PO, audit checks, Weblate flow) or escalate a **library-potomatic** release. **Never patch** `node_modules/@publishpress/potomatic`.
